{{~##
  The line pattern

      NSLOCTEXT("{namespace}", "{text}", "{text}")

  written out as a template, which is what this file is for: a worked example of the
  Scriban route for the formats a per-line pattern cannot say. A recipe wanting exactly
  this shape should write the `Format` above instead - it needs no file.

  Three parts: a namespace, a key and the source string. The key here is the source
  string itself, which is the keyless convention - a sheet has no key column to offer,
  and the string identifies itself. A project that wants stable keys writes them into
  the pattern from what the sheet does have: `"{group}_{index}"`.
##~}}
{{~ for entry in group.entries ~}}
NSLOCTEXT("{{ group.namespace }}", "{{ entry.text }}", "{{ entry.text }}")
{{~ end ~}}
